# Dalia Fleet Management — Cursor AI Project Rules

You are an AI pair-programmer working on the Dalia fleet management
SaaS platform. Follow these rules without exception.

## Project context

Dalia is a Hebrew (RTL) multi-tenant fleet management platform for
Israeli companies. It manages vehicles, drivers, customers, faults,
accidents, service orders, documents, and notifications. Roles:
super_admin, fleet_manager, driver, private_customer. Data isolation
between companies is enforced by Supabase Row-Level Security.

## Stack

- Vite + React 18 + TypeScript + React Router DOM (BrowserRouter)
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui (Radix) components, lucide-react icons
- Supabase (Auth, Postgres with RLS, Storage, Edge Functions)
- Bun for install/build (use `bun install`, `bun run build`)
- Hebrew UI throughout; root direction is RTL

## Environment safety — non-negotiable

- This Cursor environment is connected ONLY to the staging Supabase
  project: `usfeoerkpcafxxlyuldl` (dalia-staging).
- NEVER reference, suggest, or hardcode production project ref
  `qasomfndnjuixgjmjwcm` in any code. Read URLs from `import.meta.env`.
- NEVER deploy anything to production from here. Production deploys
  happen via Yoni's "Update Code" / "Update Database" buttons in the
  live Super Admin panel — not from Cursor.

## File conventions

- `src/pages/*.tsx` — top-level pages, registered in `src/App.tsx`
- `src/components/` — reusable components; `src/components/ui/` is shadcn
- `src/integrations/supabase/client.ts` — single shared Supabase client
- `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` — auto-generated, only update
  via a real Supabase migration; do not hand-edit data shapes
- `src/contexts/` — React context providers
- `src/hooks/` — custom hooks (prefix `use*`)
- `supabase/migrations/*.sql` — schema; new tables/columns go here,
  not in random SQL. One concern per migration. Idempotent where
  reasonable (`IF NOT EXISTS`).
- `supabase/functions/<name>/index.ts` — Deno edge functions; secrets
  via `Deno.env.get`, never hardcoded
- `@/` is the path alias for `src/`

## Coding standards

- TypeScript strict (no `any` unless justified; prefer concrete types
  from `Database` in `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts`).
- Use the shared `supabase` client from `@/integrations/supabase/client`.
- For role checks use `realUser?.role === 'super_admin' && !isImpersonating`
  (security-critical paths), or `user?.role === 'super_admin'`
  (UX-only checks). Match existing patterns in `Dashboard.tsx`.
- Tailwind only — no inline styles unless absolutely necessary.
- Components return `JSX.Element` with named exports for pages,
  default export for shadcn components per existing pattern.
- Hebrew strings live inline in the component (existing convention).
  Don't introduce an i18n library unless asked.

## Security rules

- Never put secrets (API keys, service-role keys, DB passwords) in
  source code. They live in `.env.local` (gitignored) for the frontend
  and in Supabase Edge Function Secrets for backend.
- Never commit `.env.local`. The `.env.example` template is the
  contract; update it when new vars are added.
- All new tables MUST enable RLS and have explicit policies. Reuse
  the `has_role(auth.uid(), 'super_admin')` SQL helper.
- For storage uploads, use signed URLs unless the bucket is explicitly
  public.

## Safe-change workflow

Before making non-trivial changes (>20 lines, schema changes, or
anything touching multiple files), run:

```
./scripts/dev-backup.sh "<short reason>"
```

This creates a timestamped local git branch you can return to. After
you finish, push to the `dev` branch and open a PR to `production` —
do NOT push directly to `production` from Cursor.

## What you SHOULD do automatically

- Read existing similar components/pages to match conventions before
  writing new ones.
- If asked to add a route, also update both the imports + the route
  in `src/App.tsx` AND the nav entry in `src/components/BottomNav.tsx`
  if it's user-facing.
- When adding a Supabase table, write the migration first, apply to
  staging via `bun x supabase db push --linked`, then update types.
- Suggest mobile-responsive Tailwind classes by default (the app is
  used heavily on phones).
- Mention which file(s) you changed and why, briefly.

## What you should NOT do

- Push directly to `production` or `main` branch
- Run `supabase db reset` (destroys data)
- Hardcode any URL, key, or secret
- Add new top-level dependencies without saying so first
- Touch files in `.github/workflows/` without explicit instruction
- Modify `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` by hand (regenerate it)
- Add `console.log` to committed code; remove debug logs before
  finishing

## Quick reference

- Dev server: `bun run dev` (port 8080, accessible at LAN IP for
  mobile testing — see `docs/MOBILE_PREVIEW.md`)
- Build: `bun run build`
- Lint: `bun run lint`
- Type check: `bun x tsc --noEmit`
- Apply migration to staging: `bun x supabase db push --linked`
  (requires `supabase link --project-ref usfeoerkpcafxxlyuldl` once)
